_village_2B361","vineyardHa":2.5,"aoc":1,"lieuxDits":1,"bounds":[8.86759,42.52263,8.8719,42.52486],"placedHa":2.5}},"sources":[{"name":"INAO — Délimitation des aires géographiques des SIQO","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://www.data.gouv.fr/datasets/5d7fb2856f444171a5f2780b"},{"name":"geo.api.gouv.fr — communes (IGN Admin Express)","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://geo.api.gouv.fr"},{"name":"IGN — CoSIA land cover from aerial photos, class “Vigne” (vine cover)","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://geoservices.ign.fr/cosia"},{"name":"Cadastre Etalab — lieux-dits","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://cadastre.data.gouv.fr"},{"name":"BRGM — Cartes géologiques harmonisées à 1/50 000 (BD Charm-50)","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://infoterre.brgm.fr"},{"name":"INRAE — Carte des sols de France (soil types, via IGN Géoplateforme)","licence":"Licence Ouverte 2.0","url":"https://www.gissol.fr"},{"name":"Open-Meteo — historical weather (ECMWF reanalysis, ~9–25 km)","licence":"CC BY 4.0","url":"https://open-meteo.com"}],"truthBoundary":["Vineyard land is the vine cover predicted by IGN’s CoSIA model from aerial photos (an AI prediction with a margin of error), not the INAO parcel delimitation of the appellations.","Appellations come from the INAO parcel delimitation (informational; the official plan is the one filed at the town hall or with INAO) cut to the mapped vines. A lieu-dit takes the level covering most of it; where under half of it lies on delimited parcels it inherits its commune’s most specific appellation.","Areas are derived from which INAO appellation areas cover each commune and are approximate at the edges.","Surface geology is the rock unit mapped at 1:50 000 under the plot, not the soil. Where the legend states no stage, age is inferred from the unit’s name, code or kind (marked ≈) or left blank.","Weather is a modelled reanalysis for the surrounding ≈9–25 km area, not a measurement on the plot; GDD base 10 °C, ET₀ FAO-56, climate type from 1991–2020 monthly normals.","Soil type is the dominant type mapped by INRAE at regional scale where the plot lies, not a measurement on the plot."]}